+  "parent_f5b_disposition": "Parent f5b GREEN stays blocked, and no resolver is added to it. Under the currently authorized coverage-corrective tests-only RED, amend RED case 11 to what is demonstrable and honest: \"Manual-review hold: no plan completion, no fence, no replacements; other authors advance; the hold is durable across restart, close and cold reopen; `issue()` fails closed for the held author; the plan completes only when the source leaves the plan at merge — by boundary settlement or by authenticated re-admission under a new `admissionEpoch` — with per-source resolution owned by D.110c-0c1f5b0x.\" Amend the matrix row `manual-review entry` the same way and add the creator carve-out from f5b0w item 2 so \"only that author stalls\" is true rather than aspirational. Add one honest line to the \"Retained findings absorbed\" list recording that per-source manual-review resolution is deferred with a named owner, matching the design's own P2 disposition rule. The parent RED's `manualReviewHold` and `displacedControls` fixtures keep their current assertions and gain: an assertion that the held `issue()` rejects with the typed settlement-held error (satisfiable only after f5b0w), an assertion that the creator still closes while a non-creator is held, and — as the honest demonstration that the plan can complete — a revoke/close/adopt/grant/close/adopt/reopen leg showing the held entry dropped at merge, the prune gate released and the empty plan fenced. That leg uses only existing authenticated product surfaces, no direct store mutation, no forged authority and no new API. Parent GREEN must not touch `writeMergedSettlementPlan`'s disposition guard, must not add any session or application member, and must not relax the fence, prune or entry-immutability rules; every one of those is f5b0w or f5b0x scope and naming it here is what keeps it from being silent expansion.",
