":[{\"severity\":\"P1\",\"title\":\"Case 25 demands unauthorized in-call owner re-activation and retry that contradicts the accepted design and has no production path\",\"evidence\":\"tests/phase-6b-d110c-0c1f5b-integration-red.test.ts:943-945 issues once and requires the call to RESOLVE for all four non-`recoveryFails` combinations (`await issue`), while :954 requires the ambiguity-time handle to be deactivated (`currentEphemeralAuthority()` undefined), :963 requires `observed.planes.get(writer.databaseName)` to be a DIFFERENT handle, :971/:975 require every later commit and publication to run under that fresh handle, :989 requires the fence/replacement to be durably present exactly once, and :1008 requires the replacement's application effect. `observed.planes` is only written by the mocked `activateCreatorSuccessorAdoption` / `reopenCreatorSuccessorAdoption` (test :132) and `activateV3LivePlane` (test :280), so the handle can only change if a full plane re-activation runs inside the single public `issue()` call. The product cannot do this: `packages/node/src/v3-live.ts:6543-6548` sets `registration.operationAdmissionHalted = true` on `ISSUANCE_OUTCOME_UNKNOWN`, `:6403-6404` then fails every subsequent local issue with `v3 operation admission is halted until recovery`, and the flag is only ever reset by constructing a NEW registration at `:8467` (`activateV3LivePlane`). `examples/v3-room/src/index.ts` has no retry/rebind/reactivate path (only `reopenCreatorSuccessorAdoption` at :2341 during session creation and `activateCreatorSuccessorAdoption` at :4227 during `adoptCreatorSuccessor`). The accepted design says the opposite: `.logs/d110c-0c1f5b0r-design-3a156aca/design.md:389` — \\\"transaction outcome unknown mid-plan | admission halts; reopen enumerates durable truth; no half-link exists\\\" — and design RED case 25 (:529-530) — \\\"admission halts; reopen finds either the row with its link or neither.\\\" The only place the in-call rebind-and-retry is stated is