e the plan declares high risk and requires a separate reviewed prerequisite for (compare D.110c-0c1d, plan :100612-100622). The design's own stop rule (`design.md:552-561`) says to stop and reslice rather than fold such behavior in. As written the continuation is unreachable after a narrow GREEN, so this blocks GREEN either as an unauthorized scope expansion or as a fixture that cannot pass.","required_action":"Choose one and record it before GREEN: (a) obtain a signed, reviewed case-25 clarification in the D.110c-0c1f5b plan record (in the style of the 62f71f4d case-24 clarification) that authorizes a bounded in-call authenticated owner re-activation plus at most one signed retry, and specifies its ownership, idempotence and failure semantics; or (b) correct `ambiguousPlanIssue` so that all four non-`recoveryFails` combinations behave as the accepted design states — the ambiguous owner halts, `issue()` rejects, and recovery is demonstrated through an explicit `fixture.reopen` that enumerates durable truth — while keeping the existing exact row-and-link-or-neither, single-retry, no-duplicate-disposition and exactly-once-effect oracles."},{"severity":"P2","title":"60,000 ms single-`it` deadline is unvalidated for a 27-case plus 64-writer composition","evidence":"tests/phase-6b-d110c-0c1f5b-integration-red.test.ts:1750 sets `60_000` for one `it` that runs the main partial-progress scenario (3 closes), `sixtyFourWriterGoldenPath()` (64 room sessions, 256 routed application issues, 6 displaced sources, 3 closes/adopts, 189 `reopen(..., transfer=true)` calls each copying two whole IndexedDB databases at :617-624, a creator cold restart and a final cold reopen), then `sameKeyReentry()` (4 closes), `manualReviewHold()`, `creatorFenceScan()` x2, `delayedPublication()` x3, `displacedControls()`, `staleLocalHead()`, `ambiguousPlanIssue()` x5 and `positiveAuthenticatedPruning()` (3 closes). The one executed calibration point is the v1 control: 1532.146791 ms for 2 rooms, 3 peers, 4 closes, 4 adopts and 3 reopens (.logs/d110c-0c1f5b-red-cecde972/result.json:35). `.logs/d110c-0c1f5b-red-cecde972/assessment.md:59` states plainly: \"No source inspection can establish total GREEN wall-clock cost; RED is not a claim that the unexecuted continuation meets that deadline.\"","impact":"If the composition exceeds 60 s the GREEN run fails on a fixture deadline rather than product behavior, forcing yet another tests-only correction commit and re-run — the exact loop that already produced two rejected runs (`1dcff170`, `8fcbc039`).","required_action":"Owner: the tests-only correction that addresses the P1. Disposition: set the `it` deadline from the measured cost of the 64-writer path (or split the composition into a second `it`), and record the measurement in the GREEN evidence. Do not change any product parameter, `maxEpochVertices`/`maxEpochBytes`, the 5,000 ms routed-ack guard, or the store page ceilings to make it fit."},{"severity":"P2","title":"Non-creator rollback-generation retention is a byte copy of the creator's AHE database, not independent per-peer evidence","evidence":"tests/phase-6b-d110c-0c1f5b-integration-red.test.ts:617-622 `reopen(..., transfer=true)` calls `transferDatabase(`${origin.databaseName}--ahe`, `${peer.databaseName}--ahe`)`, and `transferDatabase` (:366-375) does `owner.clear()` then re-puts every row of every object store — so the receiving peer's own AHE generation lineage and head are destroyed and replaced with the creator's. `positiveAuthenticatedPruning` (:1302) reopens `peers[1]` with `transfer=true` and then asserts `assertRetainedRollbackPair(peer)` for BOTH peers (:1343), and `sixtyFourWriterGoldenPath` reopens all 63 non-creators with `transfer=true` (:1241). `assertRetainedRollbackPair` (:843-859) reads exactly the copied rows.","impact":"`F5B_C13_C24C_EXACT_TWO_SUPERSEDED_ROLLBACK_GENERATIONS` and the two-level `baseExpectedHead` walk are tautological for non-creator peers: they re-read the creator's generation rows rather than proving that the peer's own successor staging/complete/swap produced and retained its own two `Superseded` rollback generations. The per-peer issuance/plan/prune oracles remain genuine (issuance and journal are not copied), so the loss is confined to case 13/24c's rollback-retention half.","required_action":"Owner: parent f5b GREEN evidence. Disposition: either assert `assertRetainedRollbackPair` only for the creator (whose AHE is never overwritten) and state explicitly that non-creator rollback retention is inherited transport state, or capture one non-creator peer that reopens WITHOUT `transfer=true` after it has independently adopted, and assert its own lineage there. Do not weaken the existing creator-side assertions."},{"severity":"P2","title":"Plan record and current-frontier at HEAD do not name the accepted corrective RED or the two rejected runs","evidence":"docs/production-hardening/production-hardening-tdd-plan-v2.md:18455-18456 still says \"Tests-only RED `3a9e9329` with evidence `f7df8f80` is causal but not yet coverage-complete\" and :18464 \"One tests-only correction must close that union before GREEN\"; the record at :100342-100350 says \"one coverage-corrective tests-only RED is authorized\". Grep of the plan for `1dcff170`, `8fcbc039`, `cecde972` and `b7751f72` returns no matches, while HEAD `b7751f72` carries the accepted evidence root `.logs/d110c-0c1f5b-red-cecde972/` (1 failed / 1 passed) plus two immutable rejected roots (`1dcff170` and `8fcbc039`, both 2 failed / 0 passed).","impact":"An agent resuming from the authoritative plan would take `3a9e9329`/`f7df8f80` as the current RED and would not learn that two focused runs were rejected and superseded, nor that three tests-only commits were needed rather than one. The evidence itself is honest (both rejected assessments are explicit and self-labelled REJECTED), so this is a record-currency gap, not a misrepresentation.","required_action":"Owner: the D.110c-0c1f5b record and