+  "causal_red_assessment": "The accepted RED is genuinely causal. `.logs/d110c-0c1f5b-red-cecde972/result.json` records one execution, runner status 1, two selected tests in one file, 1 failed / 1 passed, zero skipped/todo, zero top-level errors, no additional soft failures. The sole failure is `F5B_SETTLEMENT_PROFILE_SUCCESSOR_CODEC_REQUIRED: genuine settlement successor fails CERTIFIED_VALUE_MISMATCH before checkpoint production`, thrown at test :684 from the `close()` helper at :1672 after 417.58 ms.\n\nThe chain is real product, not a missing import/export or setup error. `openRoom(2)` builds a genuine genesis invite with `profileId: \"creator-trusted-settlement-v1\"` and a version-3 latched ACL (accepted today: packages/protocol-v3/src/latched-acl.ts:145 allows 256 members at version 3, :254 gates version 3 on `settlementProfileFor(...) === \"v1\"`). The test performs real issue, real publication through the transport, real creator ingress with awaited admission acks, and a genuine published displaced two-intent batch (`F5B_REAL_BATCH_SOURCE`, :1666) before calling `sealEpoch()`. The failure originates in production: packages/protocol-v3/src/creator-close.ts:276 (`prepareCreatorAnchorSigningRequest`) requires the literal `creator-trusted-v1`, which the seal actor maps to `CERTIFIED_VALUE_MISMATCH`, and packages/node/src/creator-close.ts:1031 throws `creator close actor failed: CERTIFIED_VALUE_MISMATCH`. The helper catches only that exact string and rethrows the labelled token; it substitutes no profile, checkpoint, signature, actor result or authority.\n\nThe five hard-coded profile sites the test pins all exist as claimed and are genuine (not synthetic-success adapters): creator-close.ts:276 (`profile.profileId !== \"creator-trusted-v1\"`), :541 (`profileId: \"creator-trusted-v1\"` in `completeCreatorSuccessor`), :598 (`decodedRecord.profileId !== \"creator-trusted-v1\"` in `openCreatorSuccessorTrust`), creator-checkpoint.ts:144 (`decoded.profileId !== ...` i