+  "scope_api_assessment": "The narrow GREEN is implementable with no new public API, wire, schema, cryptographic, dependency or threshold change — with the single exception of the P1 case-25 behavior, which is a lifecycle scope expansion rather than an API change.\n\nMinimal allowed production seams, all confirmed against current source:\n1. Five profile literal sites, replacing the hard-coded comparison with the existing exported `settlementProfileFor` predicate: packages/protocol-v3/src/creator-close.ts:276, :541, :598 and packages/protocol-v3/src/creator-checkpoint.ts:144, :242. No new export is required — `settlementProfileFor` already exists and is already consumed by latched-acl.ts:3/:254 and creator-transition-advance.ts:795/:888.\n2. Settlement checkpoint composition in packages/node/src/creator-close.ts: emit one `drp-creator-author-settlement-state` candidate and no legacy retirement/aggregate, and replace the close-aborting `AUTHOR_REENTRY_PROOF_REQUIRED` path at :530-541 with the design's fence scan under the profile only. The codec (`openCreatorAuthorSettlement`, `frontierFor`, `frontierCount`) and the advance predicate's settlement branches (creator-transition-advance.ts:795-822, :888) already exist from the closed f5b0a slice; the close-side producer is what is missing.\n3. Authenticated frontier threading: packages/node/src/v3-live.ts:8242 currently calls `readSettlementSources(registration)` with no second argument, so `settlementFrontier` is always `undefined` and the function short-circuits at :8808 — `openProgressSources` (:8822) is presently dead. GREEN must thread a checkpoint-derived `SettlementFrontierContext` (the type and its validator already exist at :4932) into that call and the classification paths at :4794/:7044.\n4. Existing-input close rebind: examples/v3-room/src/index.ts:1531-1537 currently throws `v3 room successor authority composition is unsupported` for `successorSnapshotDeclaration` + `creatorFinalitySigner`. Relaxing this un