epoch 1 with 'chain-invalid: creator checkpoint trust is invalid', which is a raw room TypeError rather than a pinned F5B token. A GREEN scoped to three sites would be rejected at its own continuation.\\\",\\\"required_action\\\":\\\"GREEN must route all five protocol-v3 sites (creator-close.ts:276/:541/:598 and creator-checkpoint.ts:144/:242) through settlementProfileFor or the genesis-bound profile carrier, emit the genesis-bound profileId in the successor and reconstructed genesis trust records, keep creator-trusted-v1 vectors byte-identical, and record the edits to f5b0a-owned files as an f5b compatibility correction. Correct the site count in GREEN evidence; do not rewrite the immutable RED assessment.\\\"},{\\\"severity\\\":\\\"P2\\\",\\\"title\\\":\\\"64-writer continuation and dedicated parent cases do not yet carry the accepted amendment's oracles; blocking for GREEN closure, not for GREEN start\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"Test lines 838-860: every one of 64 writers issues once per epoch and each ordinary issue is awaited through real creator ingress (send(), lines 334-363, 5 s admission timeout), which satisfies 'every writer contributes each epoch'. However all 63 non-creator writers stop and cold-reopen after every close (line 851), so there is no deterministic rotating cohort, none stays offline across the creator's selected restart at epoch 1 (line 852 runs after line 851), and no pending or published work crosses a boundary through plan -> fence -> replacement inside the 64-writer room (all issues are admitted before close). The only recovery oracles are frontiers.length === 64, 256 contributions and 64 distinct authors per epoch; no exact application state, ACL, authority, anchor, compact-history, plan-link or per-author/aggregate accounting assertion exists. acceptance.json honestly lists same-slot duplicate (case 23), rollback (24), delayed fence/replacement (15/16) and positive pruning gates (13) as unauthored; case 4 and cases 19-21/25 are also absent. The whole continuation shares one 60 s timeout with 189 cold reopens, each copying two IndexedDB databases.\\\",\\\"impact\\\":\\\"GREEN can be causally justified by this RED, but the parent cannot claim the 64-writer amendment or 27-case acceptance against this file as it stands; a final review would treat closure without these oracles as blocking. The 60 s budget is also at risk once the continuation actually runs.\\\",\\\"required_action\\\":\\\"Before GREEN closure, add tests-only oracles (further tests-only commits are acceptable): a deterministic rotating offline subset that contributes, stays offline across a close/adopt boundary and the selected creator restart, rejoins and contributes before the next close; selected displaced pending and published work crossing boundaries through the real plan/fence/replacement path inside the 64-writer room; exact recovered state/ACL/authority/anchor/history/plan-link/accounting assertions after restart and cold reopen; and dedicated parent cases 4, 13 (positive), 15, 16, 23, 24. Size the timeout from a measured run rather than 60 s.\\\"},{\\\"severity\\\":\\\"P2\\\",\\\"title\\\":\\\"Room input-pair relaxation must stay settlement-scoped, and the source-text pins should not carry into GREEN evidence\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"examples/v3-room/src/index.ts:1531-1537 rejects successorSnapshotDeclaration together with creatorFinalitySigner; :2415 and :2453 bind creator close only when the declaration is absent; :1630-1636 refuses a non-genesis stable floor without a declaration; the existing rebind owner is bindCurrentCreatorClose (:2466-2477, :3050-3055, :4289-4291). Both inputs already exist on CreateV3RoomSessionInput (:383, :411), so no new public API is needed. The test's legacy control (line 440) omits the signer, so a v1 relaxation of the :1531 guard would be unobserved by this file. The source reads at lines 459-474 run only inside the catch branch after the genuine CERTIFIED_VALUE_MISMATCH, so they classify rather than substitute; after GREEN a recurrence of CERTIFIED_VALUE_MISMATCH for a different reason would surface as F5B_SUCCESSOR_PROFILE_PREPARATION_V1_ONLY.\\\",\\\"impact\\\":\\\"An unscoped guard change would alter creator-trusted-v1 room behavior contrary to the design's byte-for-byte rule without any oracle noticing; the source pins could misattribute a later, different mismatch.\\\",\\\"required_action\\\":\\\"GREEN gates acceptance of the signer-plus-declaration pair and the post-reopen close rebind on settlementProfile !== 'none' (or adds a v1 retained oracle if it intentionally relaxes v1), reuses bindCurrentCreatorClose after the authenticated successor reopen rather than adding an API, and treats the three toContain pins as RED attribution only, never as GREEN evidence.\\\"}],\\\"causal_red_assessment\\\":\\\"Legitimate causal f5b RED. Both manifests validate from their directories (design 3-entry, RED 4-entry, rejected RED 3-entry); design.md and pre-review.md hashes match the plan record; the rejected manifest hashes to 304d719a… as the assessment claims. All five commits carry good signatures from key 761B99CEA81C6289, HEAD f7df8f80 equals origin, and git diff 0a09b1ca..HEAD touches only the test file and .logs (zero lines under packages/, examples/, docs/). The rejected run (0c59869a, preserved in 50a3f494) shows 2 failed / 0 passed: the raw 'creator close actor failed: CERTIFIED_VALUE_MISMATCH' at node/creator-close.ts:1031 and the room guard 'successor authority composition is unsupported' at index.ts:1537. The corrected run at 3a9e9329 (test SHA ea664e60… equals HEAD and commands.json) executed once: 1 fail / 1 pass, no runtime-error suites, file message empty, single failure message F5B_SETTLEMENT_PROFILE_SUCCESSOR_CODEC_REQUIRED thrown at test:475 from the first close at :783 after real issue, publication, creator ingress and the asserted applicationBatch displaced source (:772-779 executed before the throw). The token is emitted only when the caught