ion within f5b, not a reopening of f5b0a, provided v1 vectors stay byte-identical.\\\",\\\"api_boundary_assessment\\\":\\\"No new public API is needed. The trust-record profileId is an existing field; emitting the genesis-bound settlement identifier instead of the v1 literal, and accepting it via settlementProfileFor, is a value-domain widening already anticipated by isCreatorTrustProfile (protocol-v3/src/index.ts:839) and by node/creator-close.ts:224; the genesis anchor's profileDigest already binds the choice, so no wire, schema or authority-model change occurs. The creator cold-reopen seam uses two fields that already exist on CreateV3RoomSessionInput (creatorFinalitySigner :383, successorSnapshotDeclaration :411); the change is to stop rejecting their combination at index.ts:1531-1537 under the settlement profile and to reuse the existing bindCurrentCreatorClose owner after the authenticated successor reopen, mirroring the recovery rebind at :3050-3055. Who may close is unchanged. The v1 guard should remain unless a v1 oracle is added. The stop-and-reslice rule is not triggered.\\\",\\\"green_ready\\\":true}\",\"structured_output\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"p0_count\":0,\"p1_count\":0,\"p2_count\":3,\"findings\":[{\"severity\":\"P2\",\"title\":\"Successor-codec site inventory is incomplete: two more hardcoded creator-trusted-v1 sites sit on the cold-reopen checkpoint path\",\"evidence\":\"The RED pins protocol-v3/src/creator-close.ts:276 (prepareCreatorAnchorSigningRequest), :541 (completeCreatorSuccessor) and :598 (openCreatorSuccessorTrust), and prepareCreatorSuccessor:474-480 maps the :276 rejection to CERTIFIED_VALUE_MISMATCH, seal/src/creator.ts:379 propagates it and node/src/creator-close.ts:1031 throws — all confirmed. But protocol-v3/src/creator-checkpoint.ts:144 rejects any trust record whose profileId is not the v1 literal, and :242 rebuilds the genesis record with profileId 'creator-trusted-v1' while carrying the settlement profile bytes; protocol-v3/sr