6 refuses a non-genesis stable floor without a declaration; the existing rebind owner is bindCurrentCreatorClose (:2466-2477, :3050-3055, :4289-4291). Both inputs already exist on CreateV3RoomSessionInput (:383, :411), so no new public API is needed. The test's legacy control (line 440) omits the signer, so a v1 relaxation of the :1531 guard would be unobserved by this file. The source reads at lines 459-474 run only inside the catch branch after the genuine CERTIFIED_VALUE_MISMATCH, so they classify rather than substitute; after GREEN a recurrence of CERTIFIED_VALUE_MISMATCH for a different reason would surface as F5B_SUCCESSOR_PROFILE_PREPARATION_V1_ONLY.\",\"impact\":\"An unscoped guard change would alter creator-trusted-v1 room behavior contrary to the design's byte-for-byte rule without any oracle noticing; the source pins could misattribute a later, different mismatch.\",\"required_action\":\"GREEN gates acceptance of the signer-plus-declaration pair and the post-reopen close rebind on settlementProfile !== 'none' (or adds a v1 retained oracle if it intentionally relaxes v1), reuses bindCurrentCreatorClose after the authenticated successor reopen rather than adding an API, and treats the three toContain pins as RED attribution only, never as GREEN evidence.\"}],\"causal_red_assessment\":\"Legitimate causal f5b RED. Both manifests validate from their directories (design 3-entry, RED 4-entry, rejected RED 3-entry); design.md and pre-review.md hashes match the plan record; the rejected manifest hashes to 304d719a… as the assessment claims. All five commits carry good signatures from key 761B99CEA81C6289, HEAD f7df8f80 equals origin, and git diff 0a09b1ca..HEAD touches only the test file and .logs (zero lines under packages/, examples/, docs/). The rejected run (0c59869a, preserved in 50a3f494) shows 2 failed / 0 passed: the raw 'creator close actor failed: CERTIFIED_VALUE_MISMATCH' at node/creator-close.ts:1031 and the room guard 'successor authority composition 