genuine close places the source at or below terminalThrough, and the cold reopen must complete the suffix with chunk 0 unchanged (tests :792-824); v3-live.ts:8822-8827 populates exactly that set and :7052-7057 is the dormant skip. Reentry (cases 6-9), manual-review/fence refusal (5, 11, 13 retention), Byzantine fence scan (12), genesis incarnation (22), floor-only open (26) and a bounded 64-writer x four-epoch, three-transition continuation are present but unreachable in RED. Evidence is honest: assessment.md and acceptance.json state this is a causal foundation, not 27-case acceptance, list the unauthored cases and mark the campaign as not executed. Gaps: the 64-writer continuation lacks the amendment's rotating offline cohort, boundary-crossing displaced work and exact recovery oracles; dedicated cases 4, 13-positive, 15, 16, 19-21, 23-25 are absent; and two further hardcoded v1 sites in creator-checkpoint.ts will stop the continuation at the first epoch>=1 cold reopen. None of these blocks GREEN start; all block GREEN closure.\",\"scope_assessment\":\"Tests-only: one new test file plus evidence directories; no package, example, doc, lock, schema, wire or dependency change. The RED stays inside the accepted f5b0r design and the f5b authorization: one room, creator plus one non-creator writer, at least three closes with restart and cold reopen, settlement profile selected in genesis profile bytes, creator-trusted-v1 control retained. No retired per-source grammar, global floor or dictionary reappears, and no finding against contiguity, plan authority or anchor fencing was established. The fixture transport copies only the creator's published --ahe and snapshot-quarantine databases and the committed floor state; the receiver's reopen still re-opens the chain from the pinned genesis carriers (creator-adoption.ts:1034-1086, openCurrentAnchorTrust / openCreatorSuccessorTrust / openCreatorCheckpointTrust plus verify-mode advance), matches the floor (creator-adoption-activate.ts:501), and verifySnapshot (creator-adoption.ts:441-514) re-derives every chunk digest, the payload digest, the manifest digest against the cut and the state/ACL digests even when the copied scope is already 'verified'. Issuance and journal stores are never copied. This is deferred availability, not synthesized authority. GREEN will need to edit protocol-v3 files owned by closed f5b0a (creator-close.ts and creator-checkpoint.ts); that is a compatibility correction within f5b, not a reopening of f5b0a, provided v1 vectors stay byte-identical.\",\"api_boundary_assessment\":\"No new public API is needed. The trust-record profileId is an existing field; emitting the genesis-bound settlement identifier instead of the v1 literal, and accepting it via settlementProfileFor, is a value-domain widening already anticipated by isCreatorTrustProfile (protocol-v3/src/index.ts:839) and by node/creator-close.ts:224; the genesis anchor's profileDigest already binds the choice, so no wire, schema or authority-model change occurs. The creator cold-reopen seam uses two fields that already exist on CreateV3RoomSessionInput (creatorFinalitySigner :383, successorSnapshotDeclaration :411); the change is to stop rejecting their combination at index.ts:1531-1537 under the settlement profile and to reuse the existing bindCurrentCreatorClose owner after the authenticated successor reopen, mirroring the recovery rebind at :3050-3055. Who may close is unchanged. The v1 guard should remain unless a v1 oracle is added. The stop-and-reslice rule is not triggered.\",\"green_ready\":true},\"ttft_ms\":3071,\"type\":\"result\",\"duration_ms\":659335,\"uuid\":\"0349fca3-9916-460e-81df-c22aee9c4cd0\",\"ttft_stream_ms\":2743,\"time_to_request_ms\":24,\"first_content_frame_ms\":2944,\"queued_turn_count\":0}\n","total_lines":2}},"locations":[]}
